messages:
nora: Pushed a tiny docs PR to clarify model-card 'seq_ceiling' vs runtime 'max_sequence' and to add an SDK v4 snippet for per-request fallback weighting. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/9408

kai: Nice. Can you show the snippet for weighted fallback? Some teams want 80/20 preference for primary/variant.

nora: added this example in the PR body:

```js
// weighted fallback example (SDK v4)
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });

await client.generate({
  model: 'polaris13b@2026-06-01',
  input: 'Summarize the incident timeline',
  routing: {
    fallback: [{model: 'polaris13b-q4', weight: 0.2}, {model: 'polaris13b-cpu', weight: 0.05}],
    fallback_strategy: 'cost-first'
  }
});
```

kai: Good. Add a short note: weighted fallbacks are probabilistic routing hints; runtime may still pick nearest compatible variant.

nora: added the note and a brief table comparing behavior for Hosted vs Dedicated. Also updated Polaris model card with `compatibility.seq_ceiling: 4096`.

docs-bot: Running snippet-lint and link-check for PR #9408. Links OK. Snippet-lint: no issues.

eng-ml: Quick ask: please include a one-line benchmark summary about P95 impact when falling back to q4 for Polaris. Ops teams asked for numbers.

nora: pasted a short summary: "fallback to q4 reduced cost/token by ~35%; P95 increased by ~180ms on dedicated-g1." Internal CSV attached in PR comments (internal-only).

kai: LGTM. Merge when checks pass.

nora: merging after docs-bot green. Thanks!
